  "title": "data protection encryption signing keys secrets and rotation",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "Encryption hides content; integrity protection detects tampering. A MAC or signature can authenticate data without making it confidential.",
    "ASP.NET Core Data Protection protects payloads using purpose-isolated APIs and integrates with cookies, antiforgery, and other framework features. Shared applications need a durable, access-controlled key ring and compatible application name.",
    "Key rotation protects future payloads while old keys may still be needed to unprotect existing data. Revocation, backup, container persistence, replica sharing, and compromise response must be planned.",
    "External-service secrets, signing keys, and Data Protection keys have different purposes and lifecycles. Secure delivery, least privilege, auditing, rotation, recovery, and incident response apply to all."
  ],
